{"name":"Potter’s Pot","hex":"#845c40","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"potter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who makes pots and other ceramic wares.","One who places flowers or other plants inside their pots."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act in a vague or unmotivated way; to fuss about with unimportant things.","To move slowly or aimlessly. (Often potter about, potter around.)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potter"},{"term":"pot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Potawatomi."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat-bottomed vessel (usually metal) used for cooking food, possibly excluding saucepans (see usage notes).","The nominal household cooking vessel, metaphorically standing for the supply of food for a meal, or for the home."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pot"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"potter":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/En-us-potter.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/23/En-us-potter.ogg/En-us-potter.ogg.mp3"}],"pot":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/En-us-pot.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fe/En-us-pot.ogg/En-us-pot.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/En-au-pot.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b5/En-au-pot.ogg/En-au-pot.ogg.mp3"}]}}}